        /**
         * The attachment descriptor as BlueBubbles stores it: a plist of rustpush's own `Attachment`.
         *
         * This app used to keep its own structured map in `Attachment.metadata["rustpush"]` instead --
         * MMCS location and key as plain JSON fields -- on the reasoning that our attachment already
         * crosses FFI as a real Kotlin object, so an opaque blob bought nothing. It bought exactly one
         * thing, and it turns out to be the only one that matters here: a database inherited from
         * BlueBubbles has BB's blob in that key, our reader cast it to a Map, the cast failed, and the
         * download returned false without a word. The retry button did nothing, forever.
         *
         * So the format is BB's, both directions. `plist_to_string`/`from_reader_xml` are what BB's
